e Holder Rewards rate chosen for a coin is shown on the coin's page. It cannot be changed after launch except through a community takeover (CTO). The platform may change the flat schedule and the maximum Holder Rewards rate from time to time in accordance with Section 14 of the Terms of Use.\"}]]}]\nd7:T5d0,A creator may choose at launch to direct the Creator fee to holders of the coin instead of to the creator (a “Holder Rewards coin”; see Section 4.8 of the Terms of Use). On a SOL- or USDC-paired Holder Rewards coin, the fee paid to holders is the same tiered Creator fee as on any other coin and only the recipient changes. On a Custom Pair Holder Rewards coin, the fee paid to holders is the flat rate the creator set at launch (see “Custom Pair coins” above). Holder Rewards accumulate in a vault for the coin and are distributed from time to time, in the pool's quote asset, among Wallets holding at least the minimum eligible amount (currently US$20 equivalent) pro rata to their holdings. Before each distribution, an amount is reserved from the vault to cover the network, rent and priority-fee costs of the distribution, up to US$0.20 per eligible holder for coins paired with a token (such as USDC or a Custom Pair asset) and US$0.01 per eligible holder for coins paired with SOL; the costs actually incurred are reimbursed to the platform from that reserve and any unused reserve stays in the vault. Distributions are not run while the vault holds less than the reserve plus a minimum amount (currently US$20), or while the coin has more eligible holders than the platform's current limit. Holder Rewards are therefore paid net of distribution costs and are not guaranteed; the eligibility rules are described in the Terms of Use and in the pump.fun public documentation.8a:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4\",\"children\":\"Holder Rewards coins\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white dark\",\"children\":\"$d7\"}]]}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4\",\"children\":\"Trades routed through more than one pool\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white dark\",\"children\":\"A trade in a coin paired with another pump.fun coin may be routed through more than one pool (for example SOL to the pair coin, then the pair coin to the coin you are buying). On the pump.fun web app, mobile app and Terminal, the Protocol fee is charged once, on the first pool in the chain (the pool furthest from the coin you are trading), at that pool's rate and in that pool's quote asset; and the Creator fee (or Holder Rewards) and LP fee are charged once, on the last pool in the chain (the pool of the coin you are buying or selling), at that coin's rates and in the asset that coin is paired with. Trading interfaces that have not adopted the current pump.fun program may charge Protocol, Creator and LP fees on every pool in the route, so the total fee on such an interface can be a multiple of the rates above.\"}]]}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4\",\"children\":\"Cashback coins\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-white dark\",\"children\":\"Cashback mode is no longer available for new launches. On an existing Cashback coin, the Creator fee is credited back to the buyer as cashback where the trading interface submits the trade using the cashback instructions, and is paid to the creator where it does not; accrued cashback can be claimed through the pump.fun app. A Cashback coin may be converted into a Holder Rewards coin through a CTO.\"}]]}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4\",\"children\":\"EVM transactions\"}