mp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.050%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.200%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.300%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class="text-white dark">For all other PumpSwap pools that are non-canonical the fees are as follows:</p><div class="text-white dark"><div class="relative w-full min-w-0 overflow-auto"><table class="w-full caption-bottom text-sm"><thead class="[&amp;_tr]:border-b"><tr class="border-b border-border-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-bg-secondary/70 data-[state=selected]:bg-bg-secondary"><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Creator fee</th><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Protocol fee</th><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">LP fee</th><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Total fee</th></tr></thead><tbody class="[&amp;_tr:last-child]:border-0"><tr class="border-b border-border-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-bg-secondary/70 data-[state=selected]:bg-bg-secondary"><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.05%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.25%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.3%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section class="space-y-6"><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Custom Pair coins</h2><p class="text-white dark">A coin paired with an asset other than SOL or USDC is charged a flat fee on every trade, whatever its market cap. The Creator fee on a Custom Pair coin is fixed and is not set by the creator:</p><div class="text-white dark"><div class="relative w-full min-w-0 overflow-auto"><table class="w-full caption-bottom text-sm"><thead class="[&amp;_tr]:border-b"><tr class="border-b border-border-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-bg-secondary/70 data-[state=selected]:bg-bg-secondary"><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Venue</th><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Creator fee</th><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Protocol fee</th><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">LP fee</th><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Total fee</th></tr></thead><tbody class="[&amp;_tr:last-child]:border-0"><tr class="border-b border-border-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-bg-secondary/70 data-[state=selected]:bg-bg-secondary"><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Bonding curve</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.30%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.95%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">1.25%</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-border-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-bg-secondary/70 data-[state=selected]:bg-bg-secondary"><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">PumpSwap canonical pool</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.05%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.05%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.20%</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.30%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class="text-white dark">If the creator of a Custom Pair coin instead enables Holder Rewards at launch (see “Holder Rewards coins” below), the Creator fee shown above is replaced by a single flat Holder Rewards rate that the creator sets at launch, from 0.01% up to a maximum set by the platform (3% at the time of writing), which applies on both the bonding curve and PumpSwap; the Protocol fee and LP fee are unchanged. The Holder Rewards rate chosen for a coin is shown on the coin&#x27;s page. It cannot be changed after launch except through a community takeover (CTO). The platform may change the flat schedule and the maximum Holder Rewards rate from time to time in accordance with Section 14 of the Terms of Use.</p></section><section class="space-y-6"><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Holder Rewards coins</h2><p class="text-white dark">A creator may choose at launch to direct the Creator fee to holders of the coin instead of to the creator (a “Holder Rewards coin”; see Section 4.8 of the Terms of Use). On a SOL- or USDC-paired Holder Rewards coin, the fee paid to holders is the same tiered Creator fee as on any other coin and only the recipient changes. On a Custom Pair Holder Rewards coin, the fee paid to holders is the flat rate the creator set at launch (see “Custom Pair coins” above). Holder Rewards accumulate in a vault for the coin and are distributed from time to time, in the pool&#x27;s quote asset, among Wallets holding at least the minimum eligible amount (currently US$20 equivalent) pro rata to their holdings. Before each distribution, an amount is reserved from the vault to cover the network, rent and priority-fee costs of the distribution, up to US$0.20 per eligible holder for coins paired with a token (such as USDC or a Custom Pair asset) and US$0.01 per eligible holder for coins paired with SOL; the costs actually incurred are reimbursed to the platform from that reserve and any unused reserve stays in the vault. Distributions are not run while the vault holds less than the reserve plus a minimum amount (currently US$20), or while the coin has more eligible holders than the platform&#x27;s current limit. Holder Rewards are therefore paid net of distribution costs and are not guaranteed; the eligibility rules are described in the Terms of Use and in the pump.fun public documentation.</p></section><section class="space-y-6"><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Trades routed through more than one pool</h2><p class="text-white dark">A trade in a coin paired with another pump.fun coin may be routed through more than one pool (for example SOL to the pair coin, then the pair coin to the coin you are buying). On the pump.fun web app, mobile app and Terminal, the Protocol fee is charged once, on the first pool in the chain (the pool furthest from the coin you are trading), at that pool&#x27;s rate and in that pool&#x27;s quote asset; and the Creator fee (or Holder Rewards) and LP fee are charged once, on the last pool in the chain (the pool of the coin you are buying or selling), at that coin&#x27;s rates and in the asset that coin is paired with. Trading interfaces that have not adopted the current pump.fun program may charge Protocol, Creator and LP fees on every pool in the route, so the total fee on such an interface can be a multiple of the rates above.</p></section><section class="space-y-6"><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Cashback coins</h2><p class="text-white dark">Cashback mode is no longer available for new launches. On an existing Cashback coin, the Creator fee is credited back to the buyer as cashback where the trading interface submits the trade using the cashback instructions, and is paid to the creator where it does not; accrued cashback can be claimed through the pump.fun app. A Cashback coin may be converted into a Holder Rewards coin through a CTO.</p></section><section class="space-y-6"><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">EVM transactions</h2><p class="text-white dark">On transactions on EVM Blockchains (including Robinhood Chain), the pump.fun platform collects a fee of between 0.10% and 0.15% of the value of each transaction as part of the transaction, as described in Section 4.7 of the Terms of Use. This fee is charged in addition to the Platform Fee described under “Platform Fee” below and to the fees charged by the third-party bridge and swap provider that executes the transaction, which are not set by pump.fun. The amounts for your transaction are shown before you confirm it. The platform pays the network gas on these transactions. The pump.fun fee is set by the platform and may change.</p></section><section class="space-y-6"><p class="text-white dark">Trades placed through the pump.fun web app or the pump.fun mobile app carry the Platform Fee described below in addition to the fees above. If you access the pump.fun platform or smart contracts via another interface or platform, the Platform Fee does not apply, but you may incur additional fees charged by those interfaces or platforms.</p></section><section class="space-y-6"><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Platform Fee</h2><p class="text-white dark">From 17 October 2026, every trade you place through the pump.fun web app or the pump.fun mobile app carries an Platform Fee, in addition to the Protocol, Creator or Holder Rewards, and LP fees above, to the EVM fee described below, and to any fees charged by a third-party bridge, swap provider or network used to execute your trade (see Section 4.9 of the Terms of Use). This includes the first purchase made when you create a coin and the execution of a limit or other conditional order placed in the app.</p><div class="text-white dark"><div class="relative w-full min-w-0 overflow-auto"><table class="w-full caption-bottom text-sm"><thead class="[&amp;_tr]:border-b"><tr class="border-b border-border-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-bg-secondary/70 data-[state=selected]:bg-bg-secondary"><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0 w-1/2">Rate</th><th class="h-12 px-4 text-left align-middle font-medium text-text-secondary [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Who pays it</th></tr></thead><tbody class="[&amp;_tr:last-child]:border-0"><tr class="border-b border-border-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-bg-secondary/70 data-[state=selected]:bg-bg-secondary"><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.45% of the trade</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Trades from a wallet that has no referral code applied</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-border-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-bg-secondary/70 data-[state=selected]:bg-bg-secondary"><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">0.40% of the trade</td><td class="text-text-primary p-4 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0">Trades from a wallet that has applied another user&#x27;s referral code</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class="text-white dark">The Platform Fee is collected in the asset you spend on a purchase or receive on a sale (SOL or USDC), is deducted from the amount you spend or from your proceeds, and is shown as a separate line before you confirm a trade. For a conditional order it is charged when the order executes, at the rate that applied when you placed the order. Where you have applied a referral code, part of the Platform Fee on your trades is routed to the user who referred you (the share is set by pump.fun and may change) and the rest is retained by pump.fun; where you have not, the whole Platform Fee is retained by pump.fun. The first fee routed to a referrer&#x27;s on-chain account may be used to meet that account&#x27;s network deposit rather than being credited to the referrer. We may reduce or waive the Platform Fee for particular wallets, programmes or periods at our discretion; a reduction or waiver confers no right and may be withdrawn at any time. The Platform Fee is not charged on trades placed through Terminal or any third-party interface.</p></section><section class="space-y-6"><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Perpetuals Feature</h2><p class="text-white dark">Where you trade perpetual contracts on Hyperliquid through the Perpetuals Feature (see Section 30B of the Terms of Use), pump.fun charges a builder fee of up to 0.10% of the notional value of each order you submit (including orders that open, add to or close a position), which you approve by signature when you first use the Perpetuals Feature and which is shown as a separate line before you confirm an order, and a fee of up to 0.25% on each transfer of assets to or from Hyperliquid through the bridge made available in the app, which is charged in addition to the bridge operator&#x27;s own fees and may be shown together with them as a single bridge-fee figure. Hyperliquid&#x27;s trading and funding fees, the bridge operator&#x27;s fees and Hyperliquid&#x27;s one-time account activation fee (deducted from your first deposit) are charged by those third parties, not by pump.fun. The Platform Fee does not apply to orders submitted through the Perpetuals Feature.</p></section><section class="space-y-6"><p class="text-white dark">These fees may not be separately stated in the total transaction cost. These fees do not include fees charged by third parties which the pump.fun platform does not control, such as fees charged by wallet software or fees charged by the blockchain network (i.e. “gas” fees). The fees applicable to any transaction are determined by the pump.fun smart contracts and, for the Platform Fee, the EVM fees and the Perpetuals Feature fees, by the pump.fun trading services, and although these fees are displayed by the pump.fun web or mobile app as accurately as possible, there is no guarantee that the transaction fee(s) listed in the web or mobile app will exactly match those charged by the smart contract. The pump.fun platform may change these fees from time to time by updating this page; changes take effect when this page is updated or on any later date stated here (see Section 4.4 of the Terms of Use).</p></section></div></main><!--/&--><!--/&--><!--/&--></div><!--$!--><template data-dgst=""></template><!--/$--></div><footer class="z-[1] mt-auto border-t border-border-secondary bg-bg-primary text-text-tertiary max-md:mb-12"><div class="flex flex-col gap-8 px-[var(--padding-x-main)] pt-8 pb-4 md:hidden"><nav aria-label="Resources"><h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text-secondary">Resources</h2><ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm"><li><a href="https://swap.pump.fun" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-text-tertiary transition-colors hover:text-text-primary">PumpSwap</a></li><li><a class="text-text-tertiary transition-colors hover:text-text-primary" href="/docs/fees">Fees</a></li><li><a href="https://fees.pump.fun/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-text-tertiary transition-colors hover:text-text-primary">Revenue</a></li><li><a href="https://t.me/pump_tech_updates" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-text-tertiary transition-colors hover:text-text-primary">Tech updates</a></li><li><a class="text-text-tertiary transition-colors hover:text-text-primary" href="/docs/wallet-login-changes">Wallet sign-in changes</a></li></ul></nav><nav aria-label="Legal"><h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-text-secondary">Legal</h2><ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm"><li><a class="text-text-tertiary transition-colors hover:text-text-primary" h